@ericries, entrepreneur and author of The Lean Startup and Incorruptible, discusses the real competitive advantages across industries.

Watch the full interview on how AI is disrupting capitalism and what comes next: a video by Ksenia from Turing Post.

My slop is better than your slop. Vivek's article is an excellent example of something written with heavy AI assistance and is an absolute must-read.

Most likely, we'll be discussing it in today's newsletter. The weekend brought quite a few thoughtful posts and ideas worth unpacking. Stay tuned.

@itsreallyvivek: "Nobody really teaches you research. You get a desk, a problem someone else picked, and a vague instruction to produce something novel. So most people reverse-engineer the job from what they can see."

What if it's not junior programmers who should be worried, but corporate senior tech leads?

@Kseniase_: "Why senior talent may become both the greatest asset and the heaviest anchor in corporate AI – inspired by Satya Nadella."

A linked article explores Satya Nadella's concept of token capital versus human capital, discussing how senior talent can be both crucial and a potential bottleneck in AI development within corporations.

The most insightful conference for developers and engineers you can get. There are just a few tickets left — hurry up.

@aiDotEngineer: "The frontier labs are coming to the World's Fair. @OpenAI, @AnthropicAI, @Google DeepMind, @amazon AGI Labs, @Zai_org, and @MiniMax_AI are all on the program this year. The people building the models, in the same place as the people building on them. June 29 to July 2 in San Francisco."

The AI Engineer World's Fair 2026 is the largest technical AI conference in the world, featuring 29 tracks, 300 speakers, 100 expo partners, and over 6,000 AI engineers, founders, and VPs of AI. It runs from June 29 to July 2, 2026, in San Francisco.
